opam-version: "2.0"
synopsis:
  "Rhema: an attribute-grammar language for generating mathematics questions"
description:
  "Rhema is the question-grammar language of the RHM project. A .rhm file describes a question type as an attribute grammar whose inherited budgets set the difficulty and whose synthesized attributes compute the answer, or a whole assignment as a set of such questions. The rhema command checks a file and generates WeBWorK PG, or a paper in LaTeX or PDF, the same paper every time for the same assignment. The package installs the command and a library of grammars for arithmetic, algebra, calculus, propositional logic, sets, vectors, complex numbers, linear algebra, counting, number theory and statistics."
